## 5. Agent Orchestration Patterns

### 5.1 Subprocess Executor (`src/orchestrator/executor.ts`)

Uses `child_process.spawn` (not `exec` or `execSync`) for:
- Streaming output capture
- Proper stdin piping for context
- Per-agent environment customization
- AbortController for timeout management

```typescript
// Core execution pattern
function spawnAgent(
  command: string,
  args: string[],
  options: SpawnOptions
): Promise<ExecutionResult> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const controller = new AbortController();
    const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), options.timeout);

    const child = spawn(command, args, {
      signal: controller.signal,
      cwd: options.cwd,
      env: options.env,
      stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],  // stdin, stdout, stderr all piped
    });

    // Write context to stdin if provided, then close stdin
    if (options.stdin) {
      child.stdin.write(options.stdin);
      child.stdin.end();
    } else {
      child.stdin.end();
    }

    // Collect stdout and stderr
    let stdout = '';
    let stderr = '';
    child.stdout.on('data', (chunk) => { stdout += chunk; });
    child.stderr.on('data', (chunk) => { stderr += chunk; });

    child.on('close', (code) => {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      resolve({ stdout, stderr, exitCode: code ?? -1, truncated: false });
    });

    child.on('error', (err) => {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      reject(err);
    });
  });
}
```

### 5.2 Parallel Execution (`src/orchestrator/parallel.ts`)

For `ask_all` and `consult` with `consensus` strategy:

```typescript
async function executeParallel(
  agents: IAgent[],
  options: ExecutionOptions
): Promise<AgentResponse[]> {
  const results = await Promise.allSettled(
    agents.map(agent => agent.execute(options))
  );

  return results.map((result, idx) => {
    if (result.status === 'fulfilled') {
      return result.value;
    }
    return {
      agent: agents[idx].id,
      model: agents[idx].getDefaultModel(),
      content: '',
      durationMs: 0,
      exitCode: -1,
      error: result.reason?.message || 'Unknown error',
    };
  });
}
```

### 5.3 Response Aggregator (`src/orchestrator/aggregator.ts`)

Formats multi-agent responses into a readable comparison:

```typescript
function aggregateResponses(responses: AgentResponse[]): string {
  const successful = responses.filter(r => !r.error);
  const failed = responses.filter(r => r.error);

  let output = `## Agent Responses (${successful.length}/${responses.length} succeeded)\n\n`;

  for (const r of successful) {
    output += `### ${r.agent} (${r.model}) - ${r.durationMs}ms\n`;
    output += r.content + '\n\n';
  }

  if (failed.length > 0) {
    output += `## Failed Agents\n\n`;
    for (const r of failed) {
      output += `- **${r.agent}**: ${r.error}\n`;
    }
  }

  return output;
}
```

### 5.4 Smart Router (`src/orchestrator/router.ts`)

The router selects agent(s) based on strategy:

```
Strategy: auto
  ├── Analyze prompt keywords
  ├── If code-generation heavy → prefer codex (if available)
  ├── If explanation/analysis → prefer claude or gemini
  ├── If multiple agents available → use most-capable
  └── Fallback to first available

Strategy: fastest
  └── Select agent with lowest average latency (tracked over time)

Strategy: most-capable
  └── Select agent with highest-tier default model

Strategy: consensus
  ├── Execute all available agents in parallel
  └── Return aggregated comparison
```

