## 7. Error Handling Strategy

### Error Categories

| Category | Detection | Response |
|----------|-----------|----------|
| CLI Not Found | `which` returns null | Exclude agent from registry, log to stderr |
| Auth Failure | Exit code + stderr pattern matching | Return error with auth instructions |
| Timeout | AbortController signal | Return partial output + timeout message |
| Rate Limit | Stderr pattern (429, rate limit) | Return error with retry suggestion |
| Nesting Guard | CLAUDECODE env var detection | Exclude caller agent from available list |
| Invalid Model | Exit code + "model not found" in stderr | Fallback to default model, warn |
| Empty Output | stdout is empty after execution | Return explicit "no output" message |

### Error Response Format

All tools return errors in a consistent format within the MCP content response:

```typescript
// Error case
return {
  content: [{
    type: 'text',
    text: `[ERROR] Agent "${agentId}" failed: ${error.message}\n` +
          `Exit code: ${exitCode}\n` +
          `Suggestion: ${getSuggestion(error)}`
  }],
  isError: true,
};
```

